== 3b-1. startup validation
-ui-require-verifier bogus               -> ui-require-verifier="bogus" names no active IdentityVerifier: configure that verifier first, or drop -ui-require-verifier to keep accepting the access code over the network
-ui-require-verifier registry            -> ui-require-verifier="registry" names no active IdentityVerifier: set -ui-registry-issuer, -ui-registry-audience, and -ui-registry-keys-url first, or drop -ui-require-verifier to keep accepting the acc
-ui-require-iap -ui-require-verifier reg -> ui-require-iap and -ui-require-verifier="registry": -ui-require-iap is an alias for -ui-require-verifier=iap
-ui-require-verifier iap                 -> ui-require-verifier=iap needs an IAP audience: set -ui-iap-audience (or $GRAIN_IAP_AUDIENCE) to the IAP backend's /projects/NUMBER/global/backendServices/ID, or drop -ui-require-verifier to keep accep

== 3b-2. -ui-require-verifier=registry with the registry verifier configured
loopback bearer, no forwarding headers: 200
same bearer with X-Forwarded-For (a proxied network caller): 401
grain_access cookie with X-Forwarded-For: 401
"Enter access code" page served to a network caller: 0
{"accessCodeAccepted":true,"authenticated":false,"requireVerifier":"registry"}
grain access-code (stdout is the code, the note goes to stderr):
  stdout: xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
  stderr: grain access-code: the server requires registry (-ui-require-verifier=registry): this code is not accepted over the network, only from the daemon's own host over loopback; sign in through registry instead

== 3b-3. a server answering with a hostile verifier label
  stderr: grain access-code: the server requires verified sign-in (-ui-require-verifier): this code is not accepted over the network, only from the daemon's own host over loopback
  escape bytes on stderr: 0
